1
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:28,580
(THE YARNS)

2
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:17,640
So the latest corpse died before
the convenience store cashier?

3
00:01:18,034 --> 00:01:21,126
The cause of death was air embolism.

4
00:01:21,321 --> 00:01:24,340
They're having fun killing people.
Killer Genes.

5
00:01:24,706 --> 00:01:26,000
Arrest them as soon as possible.

6
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:31,520
Right now, the police are initially assuming
that this may be the serial killer.

7
00:01:31,763 --> 00:01:35,586
- This will be the fifth body in this case.
- Preliminary autopsy results.

8
00:01:35,662 --> 00:01:38,920
That's why the Venerable Monk has an aura
of a face full of merit. Glutathione.

9
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:42,960
- What?
- Boss is a quack doctor.

10
00:01:43,443 --> 00:01:44,688
Do you know the person in this picture?

11
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,520
Fuck!

12
00:01:55,874 --> 00:01:59,080
Normally, people who knit
will have marks on their fingers.

13
00:01:59,137 --> 00:02:02,201
Hands can't be so spotless.

14
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:03,255
The riddle on the yarn...

15
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:07,596
5/10, not coffee with cher, who am I?

16
00:02:08,591 --> 00:02:09,485
- Teacher?
- Teacher?

17
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:12,831
Miss Sookwan is very good at knitting.

18
00:02:13,495 --> 00:02:17,224
This is the yarn that Ya ordered.
I collected it and gave it to you.

19
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:19,436
And the digger we deep,

20
00:02:19,913 --> 00:02:23,480
the more everything is connected
to Sky and Sookwan.

21
00:02:26,024 --> 00:02:29,980
Yes, Miss Sookwan was invited
as a guest teacher for my club.

22
00:02:30,566 --> 00:02:33,544
And I used to be Sky's homeroom teacher.

23
00:02:33,968 --> 00:02:35,662
But we're not that close.

24
00:02:38,806 --> 00:02:40,000
Then I would like to ask you that...

25
00:02:41,415 --> 00:02:45,387
do you happen to know this person?

26
00:02:46,459 --> 00:02:47,457
Including this person.

27
00:02:49,777 --> 00:02:50,716
I know them.

28
00:03:14,921 --> 00:03:15,926
No.

29
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:17,550
Don't.

30
00:03:18,361 --> 00:03:20,281
Sky is scared. Stop that.

31
00:03:50,504 --> 00:03:51,151
What?

32
00:03:56,093 --> 00:03:57,116
Who did it?

33
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:59,100
Who did it?

34
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:00,852
Who did it?

35
00:04:17,885 --> 00:04:18,991
Are these your scissors?

36
00:04:25,335 --> 00:04:26,511
- Scissors.
- Huh?

37
00:04:26,949 --> 00:04:30,615
Sky's scissors. Sky's scissors.

38
00:04:36,643 --> 00:04:37,707
Damn you!

39
00:04:43,377 --> 00:04:45,001
Look! This is how we do it!

40
00:05:14,034 --> 00:05:15,259
You retard!

41
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,001
What happened?

42
00:05:22,142 --> 00:05:25,714
Miss, Sky threw a rock at Pakin's head.

43
00:05:32,848 --> 00:05:33,871
This person was

44
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:37,405
the one who posted the clip of Sky
throwing rocks at her friend's head.

45
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,520
It was posted on a web board
and became viral.

46
00:05:39,871 --> 00:05:42,775
At that time,
Sky received a heavy online backlash.

47
00:05:43,099 --> 00:05:44,250
But the truth is...

48
00:05:44,897 --> 00:05:47,725
Sky was bullied, wasn't she?

49
00:05:47,947 --> 00:05:51,478
At that time, no one understood
what autistic children were.

50
00:05:52,382 --> 00:05:56,556
The clip was cut and posted only to show
the part that Sky hurting her friend.

51
00:05:57,311 --> 00:06:01,012
Everyone started cursing and condemning Sky until...

52
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:05,019
Expel her. In this case,
you must expel her, Director.

53
00:06:05,154 --> 00:06:06,313
I won't allow it.

54
00:06:06,365 --> 00:06:10,083
I won't let my child study
alongside a child with a mental disorder.

55
00:06:10,518 --> 00:06:12,813
My child does not have any mental disorders.

56
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:16,017
It's your children who were bullying my child.

57
00:06:16,271 --> 00:06:18,646
Did anyone see that my child hurt your child?

58
00:06:18,890 --> 00:06:22,598
But everyone in the city saw that
this crazy kid had hurt my child.

59
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:23,819
My child is not crazy.

60
00:06:23,951 --> 00:06:28,466
If she's not crazy, then let her come out
and tell us what really happened.

61
00:06:33,106 --> 00:06:33,965
See?

62
00:06:34,553 --> 00:06:38,267
Speak up! If you're not crazy or psycho,
then speak it up!

63
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:40,253
Sky.

64
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:44,380
Sky, it's time for us
to tell the truth, sweetheart.

65
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:47,582
The truth is that it was you
who were bullied.

66
00:06:47,833 --> 00:06:51,273
Go on, Sky. Go on, Sky, come on.

67
00:06:54,779 --> 00:06:57,179
Do you see that this kid is a psychopath?

68
00:06:57,453 --> 00:07:00,180
Would we allow a psychopath to study
in the same school as our children?

69
00:07:00,674 --> 00:07:01,798
I won't accept it.

70
00:07:02,076 --> 00:07:04,584
Director, you have to expel her.

71
00:07:04,855 --> 00:07:07,000
Otherwise, I will move my child to another school.

72
00:07:07,151 --> 00:07:08,820
I will move my child to another school too.

73
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:09,760
So will I.

74
00:07:10,017 --> 00:07:12,406
- I will move my child to another school.
- I won't accept it either.

75
00:07:12,476 --> 00:07:13,892
She must be expelled.

76
00:07:14,062 --> 00:07:15,467
- I won't accept it.
- Right.

77
00:07:15,749 --> 00:07:19,307
Look at my daughter.
Today, her hair was cut like this.

78
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:23,913
How can you guarantee that my daughter's throat
will be safe from that maniac?

79
00:07:24,928 --> 00:07:26,824
- I won't accept it.
- Don't let her, everyone.

80
00:07:26,966 --> 00:07:29,540
- I won't accept it either.
- What are you going to say, Director?

81
00:07:30,233 --> 00:07:31,766
We won't accept it, Director.

82
00:07:45,979 --> 00:07:47,613
Please don't make my daughter resign.

83
00:07:47,874 --> 00:07:50,720
Please, Miss.
Sky didn't do anything wrong.

84
00:07:51,206 --> 00:07:52,928
Sky is the one who was bullied.

85
00:07:53,269 --> 00:07:54,973
Every day she got back home
with the messy uniform.

86
00:07:55,290 --> 00:07:57,502
And my hair was always messy.

87
00:08:02,935 --> 00:08:03,895
Miss Sookwan.

88
00:08:05,446 --> 00:08:07,906
I think signing the resignation...

89
00:08:08,573 --> 00:08:09,857
is way better than being expelled.

90
00:08:10,918 --> 00:08:13,126
So that she will not have a bad record
when enrolling in other schools.

91
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:17,057
Finding a school for Sky...

92
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,433
is not easy at all.

93
00:08:20,135 --> 00:08:22,911
Miss, please give Sky another chance.

94
00:08:23,606 --> 00:08:24,337
Please.

95
00:08:29,401 --> 00:08:33,133
Should you enroll Sky in the school

96
00:08:33,342 --> 00:08:34,973
for disabled children?

97
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:38,201
- In case there's a place...
- I will sign it.

98
00:09:02,493 --> 00:09:03,478
It's okay, my girl.

99
00:09:09,850 --> 00:09:13,415
We can go find somewhere else, baby.
It's okay, sweetheart.

100
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:25,266
Sky gives this to Mom.

101
00:09:26,949 --> 00:09:32,490
Sky's favorite. Mom, don't cry.

102
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,626
Sky.

103
00:09:41,314 --> 00:09:44,476
Mom, please don't cry.

104
00:09:46,313 --> 00:09:48,191
Don't cry.

105
00:09:48,946 --> 00:09:52,532
In the end, Miss Sookwan
couldn't find a school for Sky.

106
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:55,773
She had to quit her job
to take care of Sky full-time.

107
00:09:57,241 --> 00:09:58,640
I feel sorry for Miss Sookwan.

108
00:10:00,271 --> 00:10:04,587
Anyway, I would like to thank you very much
for giving us information today.

109
00:10:05,137 --> 00:10:06,424
That was nothing, we are close friends.

110
00:10:15,732 --> 00:10:18,448
Oh, wait a minute. Let me see.

111
00:10:22,403 --> 00:10:25,280
Darling, do you know the person in this picture?

112
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,375
I do.

113
00:10:29,238 --> 00:10:32,960
Nattha, the parent
who had an issue with Miss Sookwan

114
00:10:33,422 --> 00:10:35,026
She made Sky resign from the school.

115
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:38,702
In that case, do you happen to know...

116
00:10:40,535 --> 00:10:42,507
What about this person? Do you know him?

117
00:10:48,194 --> 00:10:49,046
I don't know.

118
00:10:49,384 --> 00:10:51,580
Woah, like we're totally
in a Korean drama.

119
00:10:52,313 --> 00:10:53,356
The daughter was bullied.

120
00:10:53,864 --> 00:10:55,269
The mother came back for revenge.

121
00:10:56,302 --> 00:10:58,678
Are you watching too much drama? Nonsense.

122
00:10:59,293 --> 00:11:01,728
It might be true,
that's why the code was changed.

123
00:11:02,274 --> 00:11:07,436
In fact, only us four know about this.
Besides us, there are Miss Sookwan and Sky.

124
00:11:07,909 --> 00:11:11,753
No wonder Miss Sookwan didn't want
her daughter to help us with the case.

125
00:11:12,173 --> 00:11:14,438
Then the number one suspect is Sookwan.

126
00:11:14,646 --> 00:11:17,916
She can knit, and she knows about
medical procedures and Cryptology.

127
00:11:18,024 --> 00:11:19,286
She learned Cryptology from her daughter.

128
00:11:19,648 --> 00:11:21,714
The motive for the murder was...

129
00:11:23,029 --> 00:11:25,304
the past vengeance.

130
00:11:26,535 --> 00:11:29,513
But there are two bodies
that we couldn't find the connection.

131
00:11:30,118 --> 00:11:32,866
Let's just say that everything is possible,
or maybe impossible.

132
00:11:33,492 --> 00:11:34,994
We can't overlook anything.

133
00:11:39,005 --> 00:11:39,766
Hey!

134
00:11:40,059 --> 00:11:40,709
That was...

135
00:11:41,798 --> 00:11:42,535
Don't be stingy.

136
00:11:51,029 --> 00:11:51,766
What did you say?

137
00:12:41,916 --> 00:12:43,276
Sky, what happened?

138
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:47,805
Are you shocked, Sky?

139
00:12:55,394 --> 00:12:58,309
Is this... Morse code?

140
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:06,980
And what does it say?

141
00:13:08,024 --> 00:13:09,951
"Stay the hell out of this."

142
00:13:18,758 --> 00:13:19,933
Is that a threat, Sky?

143
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:22,048
Are you afraid of a threat?

144
00:13:24,612 --> 00:13:27,697
What is a threat? Sky doesn't know.

145
00:13:28,302 --> 00:13:29,857
What is a threat?

146
00:13:30,733 --> 00:13:33,259
Then what are you afraid of?

147
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:35,613
Sky is afraid of rocks.

148
00:13:36,350 --> 00:13:37,627
I'm afraid of rocks.

149
00:13:51,895 --> 00:13:57,547
How many times have I told you
not to drag Sky into this case?

150
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:00,393
- I'm sorry.
- Sorry?

151
00:14:01,126 --> 00:14:04,780
The police held the press conference
and stated that the culprit had been already arrested.

152
00:14:05,046 --> 00:14:07,509
Then why did the culprit show up
and threaten Sky like this?

153
00:14:08,187 --> 00:14:10,584
How can I trust such authorities like you?

154
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:14,984
- But we tried our best.
- Did you?

155
00:14:15,676 --> 00:14:18,949
- It won't hurt to trust the police.
- Sergeant.

156
00:14:22,869 --> 00:14:23,822
I admitted that...

157
00:14:24,278 --> 00:14:26,240
we could catch the real culprit.

158
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,539
For your safety and sky's,

159
00:14:28,699 --> 00:14:31,180
I will send someone
to keep watch here for 24 hours.

160
00:14:53,179 --> 00:14:56,907
Or maybe we're on the wrong track.
The culprit is probably not Sookwan.

161
00:14:58,514 --> 00:14:59,846
We can't cut anyone off, Sergeant.

162
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:03,175
It might be Miss Sookwan, who caused the situation.

163
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:04,302
For what?

164
00:15:04,914 --> 00:15:08,187
If she did that,
we would follow Sky even more closely.

165
00:15:08,768 --> 00:15:12,166
And if it's really Sookwan,
it will be even more difficult to approach the victim.

166
00:15:12,779 --> 00:15:13,885
What if it's on the contrary?

167
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:17,502
It might be easier. Think about it.

168
00:15:18,765 --> 00:15:20,518
If when you Sookwan approached the victim,

169
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:23,158
she wouldn't have to worry
about Sky ruining her plan.

170
00:15:23,530 --> 00:15:26,309
And she could divert our attention to Sky instead.

171
00:15:27,481 --> 00:15:28,730
Isn't it possible?

172
00:15:29,210 --> 00:15:30,264
Oh...

173
00:15:30,866 --> 00:15:33,520
She plans to make us lost.

174
00:15:34,897 --> 00:15:36,097
That was just my assumption, Sergeant.

175
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:43,480
Let's just go with the flow for now and keep Sky safe.

176
00:15:43,923 --> 00:15:45,433
And then keep an eye on Miss Sookwan.

177
00:15:46,368 --> 00:15:47,078
Okay.

178
00:15:47,513 --> 00:15:52,584
- Then that's it. I'll follow Miss Sookwan and you...
- I'll follow Sookwan myself.

179
00:15:53,019 --> 00:15:57,360
I think if I had to live with the daughter,
we wouldn't be able to communicate.

180
00:16:00,121 --> 00:16:00,841
Okay, Sergeant.

181
00:16:01,408 --> 00:16:06,403
But I have to warn you that
you must not let Miss Sookwan know about this.

182
00:16:16,921 --> 00:16:19,394
Sky, are you feeling better now?

183
00:16:20,431 --> 00:16:21,580
Mom...

184
00:16:22,368 --> 00:16:25,180
Why did they throw a rock into our house?

185
00:16:25,673 --> 00:16:28,869
And why do we have to
"stay the hell out of this"?

186
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:34,431
What is "this"? What is it?
Why do I have to "stay the hell out of this"?

187
00:16:35,227 --> 00:16:35,951
Sky...

188
00:16:36,511 --> 00:16:40,780
It's probably about you helping the police
decode the murderer's riddle.

189
00:16:41,189 --> 00:16:43,113
I already told you to stay out of it.

190
00:16:43,815 --> 00:16:47,113
Well, Sky wanted to do it
because I wanted to know what was hidden in the riddle.

191
00:16:47,582 --> 00:16:52,514
It's fun. Sky likes it. No one has ever sent Sky
a code to decode like this.

192
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:54,090
But there is someone who doesn't like this.

193
00:16:54,546 --> 00:16:57,878
That's why they did this to us.
They're threatening us, Sky.

194
00:16:59,502 --> 00:17:00,838
What does "threaten" mean?

195
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:14,699
Verb. Verbal intimidation
or power to intimidate others.

196
00:17:15,791 --> 00:17:16,921
Verbal...

197
00:17:17,902 --> 00:17:18,963
Speaking...

198
00:17:19,589 --> 00:17:23,840
- Mom, but no one has said anything to us yet.
- Sky...

199
00:17:23,951 --> 00:17:25,857
They threw a rock into our house.

200
00:17:26,041 --> 00:17:27,874
Did it scare you, sweetheart?

201
00:17:28,323 --> 00:17:32,285
- It's like Mother is threatening Sky.
- Sky...

202
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:34,695
I didn't threaten you.

203
00:17:35,217 --> 00:17:37,683
Sky, Sky, look at my face, sweetheart.

204
00:17:38,709 --> 00:17:39,833
Please look at my face.

205
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,556
I beg you.

206
00:17:43,210 --> 00:17:46,483
If the police bring another yarn
for you to decode

207
00:17:46,653 --> 00:17:48,473
You must tell them that
you have no clue.

208
00:17:48,535 --> 00:17:50,118
You don't have to give them any more clues.

209
00:17:50,351 --> 00:17:52,299
Trust me, sweetheart. Please, Sky.

210
00:17:52,699 --> 00:17:53,850
You know, right?

211
00:17:54,723 --> 00:17:56,956
That I did it because I love you.

212
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:58,619
Baby, stay out of this.

213
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,511
Trust me, sweetheart.

214
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:02,153
Please, Sky.

215
00:18:06,139 --> 00:18:07,965
And from tomorrow onwards,

216
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:10,073
there will be police to look after you.

217
00:18:10,473 --> 00:18:11,808
You have to adapt.

218
00:18:12,226 --> 00:18:13,433
You cannot be stubborn.

219
00:18:13,843 --> 00:18:14,904
Don't be a crybaby.

220
00:18:16,281 --> 00:18:17,182
Do you understand?

221
00:18:17,732 --> 00:18:18,678
Why do I...

222
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:21,580
Stop asking. Just do as you are told.

223
00:18:21,906 --> 00:18:22,886
Do you understand?

224
00:18:23,335 --> 00:18:24,372
Do you understand?

225
00:18:25,996 --> 00:18:27,290
I understand.

226
00:18:49,638 --> 00:18:52,780
Get out, strangers are not allowed in the house, get out!

227
00:18:52,918 --> 00:18:54,441
- Get out!
- Sky.

228
00:18:55,293 --> 00:18:56,518
We already agreed.

229
00:18:56,810 --> 00:18:59,980
That the police will be watching over you
from 8:30 a.m. to 7:00 p.m.

230
00:19:00,406 --> 00:19:03,645
And there will be patrols guarding our house at night.

231
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:05,756
Last night we were threatened, remember?

232
00:19:06,580 --> 00:19:08,455
I remember. "Threaten."

233
00:19:08,935 --> 00:19:12,977
Threaten means showing intimidation
by words or power to intimidate others.

234
00:19:13,412 --> 00:19:14,128
Mmm.

235
00:19:14,615 --> 00:19:17,213
So we need a police officer to take care of you.

236
00:19:17,742 --> 00:19:19,474
So no one can throw a rock
into our house again.

237
00:19:22,187 --> 00:19:23,161
Alright, Sky?

238
00:19:24,177 --> 00:19:26,459
Please let me watch over you at this house.

239
00:19:31,328 --> 00:19:32,380
Okay.

240
00:19:36,817 --> 00:19:39,057
But wait outside the house. Do not enter the house.

241
00:19:39,415 --> 00:19:40,518
No strangers are allowed into the house.

242
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:43,106
Don't enter a stranger's house. Get out, get out.

243
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:45,019
- Get out.
- Okay, okay.

244
00:19:45,502 --> 00:19:48,681
If that's the case, I'll watch over you
from the front of the house.

245
00:19:49,464 --> 00:19:51,040
Let the police guard the front of the house.

246
00:19:51,321 --> 00:19:52,880
If you wanna go out,

247
00:19:52,946 --> 00:19:54,918
you must be accompanied by the officer.

248
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:55,940
Do you understand?

249
00:19:56,770 --> 00:19:59,565
Infringing on freedom and rights,
against human rights...

250
00:19:59,613 --> 00:20:00,360
Stop it, Sky.

251
00:20:00,410 --> 00:20:01,520
This is my final order.

252
00:20:01,902 --> 00:20:03,833
Otherwise, I will cut your allowance.

253
00:20:06,636 --> 00:20:07,593
Okay.

254
00:20:26,813 --> 00:20:28,935
I'm sorry for causing you trouble.

255
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:31,485
I thought we had an understanding since last night.

256
00:20:32,410 --> 00:20:33,206
It's okay.

257
00:20:34,118 --> 00:20:35,158
Please take good care of Sky.

258
00:20:36,278 --> 00:20:37,513
- Alright.
- Thank you.

259
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:41,718
Sky.

260
00:21:42,323 --> 00:21:43,360
Where are you going, Sky?

261
00:21:43,787 --> 00:21:44,521
Get in the car.

262
00:21:45,624 --> 00:21:47,801
It's okay. Sky will walk.

263
00:21:48,170 --> 00:21:51,853
Traveling by car wastes time and causes traffic jams,
wastes fuel and increases air pollution.

264
00:21:57,791 --> 00:22:00,125
Sky, Sky, Sky.

265
00:22:01,088 --> 00:22:02,493
You can step back a bit.

266
00:22:02,883 --> 00:22:05,853
If we walk close to each other like this,
other people will think that you are Sky's boyfriend.

267
00:22:06,104 --> 00:22:07,443
Not good. Not good.

268
00:22:08,956 --> 00:22:13,975
Sky... Do you understand the word "boyfriend"?

269
00:22:15,241 --> 00:22:17,231
Sky is autistic, not stupid.

270
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,906
Sky understands the meaning of the word "boyfriend."

271
00:22:20,292 --> 00:22:24,076
The boyfriend is a man
who you have a romantic relationship with.

272
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:31,224
Right. I'm sorry, I didn't mean it like that.

273
00:22:32,810 --> 00:22:33,720
That's okay.

274
00:22:34,132 --> 00:22:37,314
Many people understand it like you.
Sky is used to it.

275
00:22:40,643 --> 00:22:42,619
Please step back a little bit.

276
00:22:50,205 --> 00:22:51,126
Just a little bit more.

277
00:22:58,013 --> 00:22:59,853
Okay, thank you.

278
00:23:17,293 --> 00:23:20,132
If you want an autistic person
to talk to you or be interested in you.

279
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:22,605
you must first be interested
in what she is interested in.

280
00:23:22,977 --> 00:23:26,480
Try to talk about things that interest her the most
to break the ice.

281
00:23:37,412 --> 00:23:38,330
Morse code.

282
00:23:43,488 --> 00:23:44,160
Wow!

283
00:23:45,005 --> 00:23:46,817
The Morse Code is really amazing.

284
00:23:48,135 --> 00:23:51,770
I think I'm starting to want to try studying the Morse Code

285
00:23:54,612 --> 00:23:57,415
Are you also interested in Cryptology like me?

286
00:24:00,452 --> 00:24:01,662
I think it's really amazing.

287
00:24:02,253 --> 00:24:09,913
Well, Sky, if I want to start
reading a book about Morse Code,

288
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:12,111
which book should I start with?

289
00:24:15,547 --> 00:24:16,476
Here it is.

290
00:24:21,165 --> 00:24:22,994
Morse Code for Beginner.

291
00:24:29,248 --> 00:24:29,980
I'll take this one.

292
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:32,250
Sky.

293
00:24:32,723 --> 00:24:34,486
Sky has to teach me too.

294
00:24:44,754 --> 00:24:46,100
Do you want a lollipop?

295
00:24:49,401 --> 00:24:50,267
Buy it then.

296
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:54,920
My mother set a quota
to buy only one lollipop per day.

297
00:24:56,062 --> 00:24:58,243
But it's really hard to choose.

298
00:24:59,711 --> 00:25:01,979
Then let's take these three.

299
00:25:02,180 --> 00:25:05,756
No, my mother doesn't allow me
to accept things from strangers.

300
00:25:07,634 --> 00:25:08,598
I'll take these too, please

301
00:25:09,506 --> 00:25:10,706
I'm not a stranger, Sky.

302
00:25:11,206 --> 00:25:15,443
Now I am a student
who will learn Cryptology from you.

303
00:25:16,128 --> 00:25:19,707
These lollipops are considered tuition fees, okay?

304
00:25:22,361 --> 00:25:23,920
This deal is interesting.

305
00:25:26,702 --> 00:25:27,460
Scan and pay.

306
00:25:36,177 --> 00:25:37,499
We are friends now.

307
00:25:39,175 --> 00:25:40,121
No, it's not.

308
00:25:40,379 --> 00:25:44,076
We just changed our status from strangers
to acquaintances.

309
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:54,170
Thank you, officer.

310
00:25:54,963 --> 00:25:55,718
Pleasure.

311
00:26:01,008 --> 00:26:01,815
Thank you.

312
00:26:47,740 --> 00:26:51,725
Dash-dot-dot, another L, and a dot.

313
00:27:25,426 --> 00:27:26,380
Wrong.

314
00:27:28,605 --> 00:27:29,944
Is this the letter O?

315
00:27:35,916 --> 00:27:36,760
Hello.

316
00:27:37,996 --> 00:27:38,920
Hello.

317
00:27:44,380 --> 00:27:45,951
Three long signals.

318
00:27:46,173 --> 00:27:48,038
O is three long signals.

319
00:28:13,864 --> 00:28:15,259
It's okay, officer.

320
00:28:30,556 --> 00:28:31,400
Thank you.

321
00:28:40,382 --> 00:28:41,980
Two seven, officer.

322
00:28:57,328 --> 00:28:58,351
Wrong.

323
00:28:58,660 --> 00:29:00,535
Do you still can't remember?

324
00:29:01,180 --> 00:29:02,059
Let's do it again.

325
00:29:02,702 --> 00:29:03,840
Nine-one-five

326
00:29:11,864 --> 00:29:14,758
Don't peek, officer. Don't cheat.

327
00:29:20,010 --> 00:29:20,636
Nine.

328
00:29:23,980 --> 00:29:24,535
Nine.

329
00:29:28,702 --> 00:29:29,440
One.

330
00:29:34,140 --> 00:29:34,709
Five.

331
00:29:36,942 --> 00:29:38,260
Three one eight.

332
00:29:39,328 --> 00:29:41,154
Three one eight

333
00:29:42,750 --> 00:29:43,829
No cheating.

334
00:30:00,493 --> 00:30:02,615
Sky, why don't you buy a lollipop today?

335
00:30:03,926 --> 00:30:07,380
Mom knew that you bought me
several lollipops at once.

336
00:30:07,551 --> 00:30:11,339
My mom wasn't okay with it
and wouldn't let Sky eat lollipops for a week.

337
00:30:11,707 --> 00:30:13,300
Oh Sky, if that's the case,

338
00:30:13,429 --> 00:30:15,520
you should not let your mom see you eat them.
Come on, I'll buy it for you.

339
00:30:16,003 --> 00:30:19,377
You are a police officer,
why do you teach people to break the rules?

340
00:30:25,036 --> 00:30:27,412
Have you ever watched the movie, <i>Parasite</i>?

341
00:30:27,996 --> 00:30:29,980
Yes, it was very famous and even won an Oscar.

342
00:30:30,507 --> 00:30:35,325
Yes, Sky likes it a lot because
Morse Code is used in the movie.

343
00:30:35,558 --> 00:30:37,332
The uncle who turns the lights
on and off, isn't he?

344
00:30:51,248 --> 00:30:53,373
Do you still not memorize all the codes?

345
00:30:53,836 --> 00:30:57,707
Sky, I can't even remember all the numbers.

346
00:30:57,805 --> 00:31:01,474
There are so many letters. Please give me
some time to memorize them.

347
00:31:27,224 --> 00:31:28,723
What did you buy, officer?

348
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:30,946
Here.

349
00:31:36,900 --> 00:31:37,881
No thanks.

350
00:31:38,380 --> 00:31:41,533
If Mom knew, Mom wouldn't let Sky
have lollipops anymore.

351
00:31:41,930 --> 00:31:44,038
- No thanks.
- Sky, don't let you...

352
00:31:46,977 --> 00:31:51,580
Well, consider this as a teaching tool.

353
00:31:51,972 --> 00:31:55,499
So now you will teach me the code, right?

354
00:31:55,590 --> 00:32:01,770
I'm your student
and would like to leave this to you.

355
00:32:02,584 --> 00:32:03,580
Is this alright?

356
00:32:06,500 --> 00:32:08,775
Here. We can do it like this.

357
00:32:09,580 --> 00:32:12,619
Dash-dash-dash-dash-dot.

358
00:32:14,278 --> 00:32:15,046
It equals nine.

359
00:32:17,120 --> 00:32:18,052
That's correct.

360
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:20,754
I'll leave it to you, Miss Sky.

361
00:32:22,994 --> 00:32:25,826
Consider it a teaching tool.

362
00:32:39,481 --> 00:32:40,780
Thank you, officer.

363
00:36:48,393 --> 00:36:51,328
- Is that The Yarn Murderer?
- Yes. Here's the yarn.

364
00:36:57,580 --> 00:37:01,320
The body of a young woman was found
brutally murdered with dismemberment.

365
00:37:01,509 --> 00:37:05,314
Then the internal organs of the
deceased were piled up next to the body.

366
00:37:05,460 --> 00:37:09,676
In addition, the police also found
important evidence that showed that

367
00:37:09,753 --> 00:37:14,351
this case is related to a serial killer case
that was recently closed.

368
00:37:17,560 --> 00:37:21,440
Sir, can I have an interview, please?
So this case is the same as a serial killer case, right?

369
00:37:21,560 --> 00:37:23,920
- Isn't that right?
- But you stated that the case was closed.

370
00:37:24,073 --> 00:37:26,520
Can you confirm that the previous culprit
who died was a scapegoat?

371
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:27,640
Is that right?

372
00:37:42,880 --> 00:37:44,920
(Great! The police let the murderer on the loose.
How could we go on living like this? So scary.)

373
00:37:44,950 --> 00:37:46,198
( I feel so sorry for the scapegoat. He died in vain.)

374
00:37:46,240 --> 00:37:47,760
(Seriously? How could the police bullshit to our faces?
Police sucks. Who can guarantee our safety?)

375
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:52,200
(Do people mean anything to you? We're not stupid,
we aren't eating taxes like those suckers in the PD.)

376
00:37:52,869 --> 00:37:53,617
(Do people mean anything to the police?)

377
00:37:53,680 --> 00:37:54,824
(I really feel sorry for the scapegoat.)

378
00:37:54,880 --> 00:37:55,666
(How long do we have to
live with the murderer among us?)

379
00:37:55,720 --> 00:37:56,320
(Who can guarantee our safety?
Who is responsible for this?

380
00:37:56,840 --> 00:37:57,880
(Do you see us people that stupid, you asshole?)

381
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:11,217
Do you see how heavily the PD
receives the backlash? Read it.

382
00:38:11,940 --> 00:38:15,273
I told you from the beginning that that quack doctor is unlikely to be the real murderer.

383
00:38:15,398 --> 00:38:16,780
Yeah, I know.

384
00:38:17,102 --> 00:38:20,160
I have to make such a statement because
the high-ups ordered me to.

385
00:38:20,511 --> 00:38:22,413
And one of the high-ups is your father.

386
00:38:22,813 --> 00:38:25,965
What does Dr. Chonlathorn
have to do with the press conference, sir?

387
00:38:26,246 --> 00:38:27,488
What about him?

388
00:38:28,097 --> 00:38:30,622
Well, that culprit had Killer Genes.

389
00:38:31,040 --> 00:38:33,580
That's it. Just because he had Killer Genes,
everyone believes it's him.

390
00:38:33,986 --> 00:38:34,817
That's all.

391
00:38:35,241 --> 00:38:38,045
But I used to be a policeman, I know it's not true.

392
00:38:48,299 --> 00:38:49,005
Yes, sir.

393
00:38:52,031 --> 00:38:52,713
What?

394
00:38:54,066 --> 00:38:55,033
Yes, sir. Don't worry.

395
00:38:56,281 --> 00:38:57,186
I'll take care of it for you.

396
00:38:59,860 --> 00:39:01,460
They'll have you on a TV show.

397
00:39:01,822 --> 00:39:03,547
Even though the real culprit hasn't been caught yet.

398
00:39:05,019 --> 00:39:05,923
They obviously send us for a death sentence.

399
00:39:07,366 --> 00:39:08,883
Being on TV is one thing,

400
00:39:09,460 --> 00:39:12,664
but now, finding the murderer
is the most important thing.

401
00:39:13,433 --> 00:39:15,880
We send people to follow Miss Sookwan
all the time,

402
00:39:16,160 --> 00:39:20,166
but there are still deaths.
It means that Sookwan is not a murderer.

403
00:39:20,838 --> 00:39:22,612
One more thing that we are curious about is that...

404
00:39:23,074 --> 00:39:26,285
the victim wasn't a teacher
like what was told in the riddle.

405
00:39:26,886 --> 00:39:29,346
- The murderer may change their mind.
- No way.

406
00:39:30,448 --> 00:39:33,015
This type of murderer always has a clear goal.

407
00:39:33,749 --> 00:39:36,100
They're sending a message to someone.

408
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:38,723
They definitely won't change the plan.

409
00:39:40,205 --> 00:39:42,907
And now, it's already more than
halfway through killing six people.

410
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:44,525
They are confident.

411
00:39:45,297 --> 00:39:46,222
They are boisterous.

412
00:39:46,747 --> 00:39:48,215
Thinking that they are above the police

413
00:39:52,459 --> 00:39:53,641
Or did we solve the riddle wrong?

414
00:39:55,005 --> 00:39:55,944
"Not coffee with cher."

415
00:39:56,834 --> 00:39:58,246
It might not be a teacher.

416
00:40:15,342 --> 00:40:16,438
- Miss?
- Huh.

417
00:40:16,514 --> 00:40:19,318
Why is it full of holes when I knit it?

418
00:40:19,474 --> 00:40:24,928
Well, in knitting, you have to
count the stitches in each row.

419
00:40:25,266 --> 00:40:31,610
And if any of the stitches fall out or are out of line,
if you make a mistake, it will become a hole like this.

420
00:40:31,930 --> 00:40:34,406
You see, we have to start it all over again.

421
00:40:35,686 --> 00:40:38,629
- Miss, what are you doing?
- You must undo it all.

422
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:40,337
Try again.

423
00:40:40,549 --> 00:40:42,055
Tell me when you are done undoing it.

424
00:40:42,243 --> 00:40:44,194
Go ahead, we'll start a new pattern soon.

425
00:40:48,883 --> 00:40:49,947
What are you doing?

426
00:40:51,850 --> 00:40:53,405
Have you seen the news, Miss Sookwan?

427
00:40:53,916 --> 00:40:54,928
What news?

428
00:40:55,043 --> 00:40:58,751
They said that the person who was killed yesterday
was a victim of a serial killer.

429
00:40:59,742 --> 00:41:03,227
So the person who died wasn't the real culprit?

430
00:41:04,382 --> 00:41:06,236
And what the police announced was...

431
00:41:08,191 --> 00:41:11,589
It's not surprising at all. That's how the police are.

432
00:41:11,718 --> 00:41:13,283
If the criminals were caught easily,

433
00:41:13,666 --> 00:41:15,954
there probably wouldn't be
a continuous killing like this.

434
00:41:16,486 --> 00:41:20,789
- Oh, really?
- Miss, I've finished.

435
00:41:21,160 --> 00:41:23,760
- Excuse me.
- Alright.

436
00:41:28,733 --> 00:41:33,060
From now on, you must knit every stitch.

437
00:41:33,850 --> 00:41:36,017
You can't miss a single stitch.

438
00:41:37,353 --> 00:41:38,274
Start it all over again.

439
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:57,000
The sex worker...

440
00:42:08,960 --> 00:42:09,920
What the hell?

441
00:43:14,810 --> 00:43:15,513
Nawin

442
00:43:16,288 --> 00:43:18,674
I think I saw tire marks at the scene of the accident.

443
00:43:19,408 --> 00:43:21,412
Please check for me what brand it is,

444
00:43:22,059 --> 00:43:22,977
and what car uses that tire.

445
00:44:02,994 --> 00:44:07,224
Sky, today I have a new code
for you to help me decode.

446
00:44:08,060 --> 00:44:09,784
- Do you want to help me?
- Code.

447
00:44:10,278 --> 00:44:11,353
Good, good.

448
00:44:11,412 --> 00:44:13,812
Sky wants to help you, officer.
Where is it?

449
00:44:25,843 --> 00:44:26,886
I beg you...

450
00:44:27,520 --> 00:44:30,838
If the police bring another yarn
for you to decode

451
00:44:31,015 --> 00:44:32,845
You must tell them that
you have no clue.

452
00:44:33,036 --> 00:44:34,413
You don't have to give them any more clues.

453
00:44:34,681 --> 00:44:36,720
Trust me, sweetheart. Please, Sky.

454
00:44:40,726 --> 00:44:44,337
My mother said that if the police come
to ask about the code on the yarn again,

455
00:44:44,470 --> 00:44:45,659
I must tell them that I don't know.

456
00:44:45,798 --> 00:44:46,580
Sky doesn't know.

457
00:44:46,780 --> 00:44:48,688
My mother told me to say that I don't know.

458
00:44:49,391 --> 00:44:50,880
What did your mother say?

459
00:44:51,580 --> 00:44:54,770
My mother said that if the police come
to ask about the code on the yarn again,

460
00:44:54,800 --> 00:44:55,930
I must tell them that I don't know.

461
00:44:56,747 --> 00:44:57,446
Why?

462
00:44:58,006 --> 00:44:59,373
I don't know.

463
00:45:00,146 --> 00:45:07,568
No, I mean why did your mom
tell you not to help me decode?

464
00:45:08,222 --> 00:45:13,610
I don't know. That's all my mom told me.
Officer, please stop meddling in Sky and Mom's business.

465
00:45:17,339 --> 00:45:20,667
Can Sky go now?
The lady at the noodle shop is waiting.

466
00:45:21,756 --> 00:45:22,333
Okay.

467
00:45:23,902 --> 00:45:24,646
Please.

468
00:45:36,486 --> 00:45:39,666
- In the southern dialect, it is called Nom Jeen.
- In the southern dialect, it is called Nom Jeen.

469
00:45:39,740 --> 00:45:41,829
Same usual, right? Take a seat.

470
00:45:45,405 --> 00:45:46,240
Beef curry as usual.

471
00:46:15,401 --> 00:46:16,267
SOS.

472
00:46:17,290 --> 00:46:20,932
What's wrong with you, officer?
Is there anything Sky can help you with?

473
00:46:22,100 --> 00:46:22,834
Of course, there is.

474
00:46:23,693 --> 00:46:25,871
I have something I'd like Sky to help me with.

475
00:46:26,998 --> 00:46:28,420
But if it's about decoding...

476
00:46:29,300 --> 00:46:31,880
Sky can't do it. Mom told me not to.

477
00:46:32,380 --> 00:46:33,961
Sky can't help you.

478
00:46:39,732 --> 00:46:41,600
- Here you are.
- Thank you.

479
00:46:48,347 --> 00:46:49,102
Sky.

480
00:46:50,987 --> 00:46:52,692
Sky was bullied.

481
00:46:53,760 --> 00:46:55,652
Have someone ever thrown a rock at you?

482
00:46:58,013 --> 00:47:00,563
I was bullied too.

483
00:47:01,360 --> 00:47:02,577
That's why I became a police officer.

484
00:47:03,140 --> 00:47:04,626
So that I can help other people.

485
00:47:06,500 --> 00:47:08,994
Sky, don't you want to help those who are being bullied?

486
00:47:12,994 --> 00:47:13,867
Please, Sky.

487
00:47:14,800 --> 00:47:18,020
Sky, can you please take a look at this piece of yarn?

488
00:47:18,761 --> 00:47:20,121
Is there a hidden code?

489
00:47:21,965 --> 00:47:22,862
Please, Sky.

490
00:47:24,073 --> 00:47:26,090
Everyone is waiting for Sky to help.

491
00:47:47,325 --> 00:47:48,365
Sky.

492
00:47:48,824 --> 00:47:51,040
I don't have time to decode it right now.

493
00:48:02,048 --> 00:48:03,580
Is there something like this, Sky?

494
00:48:13,707 --> 00:48:14,664
Okay.

495
00:48:15,123 --> 00:48:16,118
I promise.

496
00:48:16,827 --> 00:48:20,139
This matter will be kept a secret between the two of us.

497
00:48:53,980 --> 00:48:54,800
Here it is.

498
00:49:10,723 --> 00:49:14,539
There is no code.
This yarn does not have a code.

499
00:49:17,412 --> 00:49:19,095
No code at all?

500
00:49:23,433 --> 00:49:24,253
Thank you.

501
00:49:31,071 --> 00:49:34,132
What the heck, there's no code in that yarn?

502
00:49:34,483 --> 00:49:35,513
I'm sure

503
00:49:36,330 --> 00:49:39,440
- That Sky definitely won't lie to us.
- Are you sure, Inspector?

504
00:49:40,413 --> 00:49:42,486
What if Sky lied to you, as her mother told her to?

505
00:49:44,271 --> 00:49:47,109
Let's just say I'll send someone
to take care of Sky after me.

506
00:49:47,666 --> 00:49:48,646
I'll send you the location.

507
00:49:49,180 --> 00:49:50,636
Then you can meet me at the show.

508
00:50:09,262 --> 00:50:10,229
Hello, viewers.

509
00:50:10,292 --> 00:50:14,320
For the hot topics that we will discuss today,

510
00:50:14,380 --> 00:50:16,100
it can't be anything else

511
00:50:16,309 --> 00:50:20,313
but the matter of arresting the scapegoat
for the serial killer murder case.

512
00:50:20,626 --> 00:50:25,711
Today we will be talking to the head
of the special investigation unit of this case.

513
00:50:26,240 --> 00:50:29,400
And this is Police Lieutenant Colonel Pilanthorn Traikanon.
Welcome, Sir.

514
00:50:29,638 --> 00:50:30,323
Great to be here.

515
00:50:31,300 --> 00:50:32,083
This is the inspector.

516
00:50:32,313 --> 00:50:33,471
- Right.
- Did I call you correctly?

517
00:50:33,710 --> 00:50:34,240
That's right.

518
00:50:34,320 --> 00:50:37,391
Okay, let me ask you my first question in a very straightforward manner, Inspector.

519
00:50:37,742 --> 00:50:40,956
Are the police arresting the scapegoat? Please be honest.

520
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:45,057
It would not be quite right to call it a scapegoat.

521
00:50:45,680 --> 00:50:46,493
Eh...

522
00:50:46,817 --> 00:50:48,210
- Isn't that right?
- Yes.

523
00:50:48,270 --> 00:50:49,582
Then what would be right, Inspector?

524
00:50:49,829 --> 00:50:54,431
First of all, I must inform you that the suspect who died

525
00:50:54,566 --> 00:50:59,980
At first, the police thought he was the real murderer
due to the evidence and circumstantial witness

526
00:51:00,344 --> 00:51:03,140
Including the day the monk was murdered,

527
00:51:03,387 --> 00:51:05,899
This suspect was also at the scene.

528
00:51:06,253 --> 00:51:07,092
Wait a minute, Inspector.

529
00:51:07,613 --> 00:51:11,276
You used the word... "suspect."

530
00:51:11,735 --> 00:51:13,551
- He's not a murderer.
- Yes.

531
00:51:14,027 --> 00:51:15,770
Then who is the murderer?

532
00:51:16,827 --> 00:51:22,827
To be honest, we still can't say for sure who the real murderer is, as I just told you...

533
00:51:22,960 --> 00:51:28,142
this suspect was arrested suspiciously
and died while we were making the arrest.

534
00:51:28,459 --> 00:51:30,998
Which means the murderer cannot be identified.

535
00:51:31,485 --> 00:51:35,269
Then why did the police have to rush
to announce the closing of the case like that?

536
00:51:35,520 --> 00:51:38,097
Because recently, one more victim has died, Inspector.

537
00:51:38,629 --> 00:51:43,600
It's like the police arrested the scapegoat
and lied to the people.

538
00:51:44,653 --> 00:51:48,132
Oh, you crazy! If you're gonna talk like that,
let's just shoot me now.

539
00:51:54,166 --> 00:51:58,313
I would like to apologize to all Thai citizens.
It was all my fault.

540
00:51:58,720 --> 00:51:59,980
I accept all responsibility.

541
00:52:00,754 --> 00:52:02,246
But I promise you that...

542
00:52:02,619 --> 00:52:05,130
I will arrest the real murderer

543
00:52:05,634 --> 00:52:08,678
and take legal action on them as soon as possible.

544
00:52:09,467 --> 00:52:10,824
Look at that.

545
00:52:11,335 --> 00:52:12,486
The inspector receives a heavy backlash.

546
00:52:13,360 --> 00:52:15,022
"Police sucks."

547
00:52:15,478 --> 00:52:17,641
- How could you...
- Shut up! Mark, Stop!

548
00:52:17,913 --> 00:52:20,960
In a moment, I will have a phone-in.

549
00:52:21,495 --> 00:52:24,309
Let the people call in
and ask the inspector for the truth.

550
00:52:24,382 --> 00:52:25,906
Are you okay with this?

551
00:52:26,460 --> 00:52:27,373
My pleasure.

552
00:52:27,680 --> 00:52:31,144
Oh, Lan, if there's a phone-in, you'll be in big trouble.

553
00:52:31,880 --> 00:52:34,591
But one last question, Inspector.

554
00:52:35,196 --> 00:52:39,259
Since the case has been filed, the police...

555
00:52:39,920 --> 00:52:41,530
has any progress yet?

556
00:52:42,640 --> 00:52:48,438
I have to say here that
the real culprit left some evidence,

557
00:52:48,950 --> 00:52:51,311
That challenged the police at the crime scene.

558
00:52:51,954 --> 00:52:55,579
How did they challenge the police? Please explain.

559
00:52:55,735 --> 00:53:00,121
As we all know, most serial killers
have Killer Genes in them.

560
00:53:00,546 --> 00:53:04,780
These murderers will do anything to achieve certain goals.

561
00:53:05,304 --> 00:53:07,617
And this murderer is the same.

562
00:53:10,511 --> 00:53:13,784
- Hey, that's a yarn?
- That's right.

563
00:53:14,344 --> 00:53:17,161
The perpetrator left evidence at the scene of the crime.

564
00:53:17,631 --> 00:53:22,615
It's a yarn with a riddle leading to their next victim.

565
00:53:24,222 --> 00:53:29,763
This means that the police know
who is likely to be the victim.

566
00:53:30,226 --> 00:53:30,900
That's right.

567
00:53:40,229 --> 00:53:43,220
Inspector, broadcasting in fifteen minutes.

568
00:53:43,680 --> 00:53:46,417
- When you're ready, please.
- Alright.

569
00:53:59,725 --> 00:54:00,504
Yes, father.

570
00:54:01,273 --> 00:54:05,947
You can't admit defeat,
those with Killer Genes will be very happy,

571
00:54:06,459 --> 00:54:08,097
if they knew we were going to lose.

572
00:54:09,377 --> 00:54:12,608
You have to know what the murderer is up to,
you have to look down and despise them.

573
00:54:13,085 --> 00:54:15,620
That they are the ones who are about to lose.

574
00:54:16,295 --> 00:54:19,422
And then you take this opportunity to pressure them.

575
00:54:19,940 --> 00:54:22,260
Until they cannot bear it and reveal their identity.

576
00:54:24,219 --> 00:54:26,800
I hope you won't disappoint me, will you?

577
00:54:29,777 --> 00:54:32,142
I would like to take
this opportunity to ask for permission

578
00:54:32,619 --> 00:54:36,055
- To communicate with the murderer.
- Please do.

579
00:54:38,059 --> 00:54:39,481
The second camera is on the inspector's face.

580
00:54:42,615 --> 00:54:43,673
I know you're watching.

581
00:54:46,608 --> 00:54:52,240
You're stupid to think that the police didn't realize that you left a riddle in the yarn.

582
00:54:52,615 --> 00:54:54,744
So you had to change the riddle.

583
00:54:55,029 --> 00:54:57,720
If you're such a fearless one,
why would you change it then?

584
00:54:58,493 --> 00:54:59,777
Because you're scared.

585
00:55:04,890 --> 00:55:08,598
There is no code. This yarn does not have a code.

586
00:55:09,078 --> 00:55:12,880
You were afraid that the police would find out,
so you had to change.

587
00:55:13,133 --> 00:55:15,092
Change the riddle on the yarn,

588
00:55:15,913 --> 00:55:17,133
and change the victim.

589
00:55:17,540 --> 00:55:22,664
You had a particular style of killing because you were
afraid that the police would find you first.

590
00:55:22,780 --> 00:55:24,490
You were just afraid of that.

591
00:55:25,502 --> 00:55:26,946
It's like you've already lost.

592
00:55:27,777 --> 00:55:31,680
Now you're just... a loser murderer,

593
00:55:32,907 --> 00:55:33,707
otherwise,

594
00:55:35,248 --> 00:55:37,036
you're not the real murderer.

595
00:55:41,360 --> 00:55:42,840
No!

596
00:56:02,100 --> 00:56:05,373
I am the real murderer.

597
00:56:08,560 --> 00:56:10,977
Lieutenant, the culprit contacted us.

598
00:56:13,892 --> 00:56:14,789
Sir,

599
00:56:15,193 --> 00:56:17,586
There's a claiming culprit who wants
to connect the phone-in for the show.

600
00:56:17,899 --> 00:56:20,017
It seems like there's an incoming call now.

601
00:56:20,080 --> 00:56:21,833
Anyway, let's cut to the studio now.

602
00:56:22,497 --> 00:56:24,229
Okay, connect to the phone-in

603
00:56:24,928 --> 00:56:25,480
Alright.

604
00:56:36,671 --> 00:56:40,780
- Who are you? Wait, what's your name?
- It's me.

605
00:56:41,328 --> 00:56:43,815
The serial killer you guys are looking for.

606
00:56:47,165 --> 00:56:48,476
How can I be sure?

607
00:56:48,963 --> 00:56:51,182
That you are the real murderer
and not just calling to prank me.

608
00:56:52,674 --> 00:56:55,040
Noppachai, Nattha,

609
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:58,083
Isriya, Anon,

610
00:56:58,528 --> 00:56:59,360
Phongsak,

611
00:56:59,980 --> 00:57:00,806
Naphat.

612
00:57:01,582 --> 00:57:05,000
Did I call out the names of the victims
in the correct order?

613
00:57:08,180 --> 00:57:10,542
Isn't it a bit too easy just to call out the names?

614
00:57:11,280 --> 00:57:15,064
Just by watching the news or searching the internet, you can probably get all the names of the victims.

615
00:57:15,960 --> 00:57:16,751
It's too easy

616
00:57:16,800 --> 00:57:18,918
to confirm that you are the real murderer.

617
00:57:22,180 --> 00:57:24,549
Please delay him a little longer, Inspector.
We still can't get a signal.

618
00:57:25,676 --> 00:57:28,017
Could you please confirm...

619
00:57:28,295 --> 00:57:31,180
how do you choose the victims?

620
00:57:31,840 --> 00:57:32,699
Fool!

621
00:57:33,520 --> 00:57:36,316
If I told you, why would I leave a riddle?

622
00:57:37,920 --> 00:57:39,537
You said you were smart.

623
00:57:41,589 --> 00:57:42,754
Catch me if you can.

624
00:57:43,492 --> 00:57:44,594
Catch me!

625
00:57:45,770 --> 00:57:46,650
A riddle?

626
00:57:47,179 --> 00:57:48,605
Are you still talking about riddles?

627
00:57:49,036 --> 00:57:52,838
Since your latest victim doesn't match
the latest riddle you left.

628
00:57:53,579 --> 00:57:57,780
Or maybe you never knew about
any riddles in the yarn, right?

629
00:57:58,184 --> 00:58:01,878
That's right, you never know
about any riddles in the yarn.

630
00:58:02,754 --> 00:58:05,206
Because you are not the real murderer.

631
00:58:06,360 --> 00:58:11,000
No way, I'm the real killer!

632
00:58:13,078 --> 00:58:16,490
I am the murderer.

633
00:58:16,706 --> 00:58:17,255
Are you?

634
00:58:17,819 --> 00:58:20,177
Then can you confirm or do you have any evidence

635
00:58:20,240 --> 00:58:22,560
that can identify you as the real murderer?

636
00:58:23,043 --> 00:58:23,641
Where is it?

637
00:58:23,980 --> 00:58:25,120
Can I see some evidence?

638
00:58:25,749 --> 00:58:28,041
Evidence? Sure.

639
00:58:30,132 --> 00:58:32,187
Are you trying to test me?

640
00:58:40,361 --> 00:58:41,240
Look!

641
00:58:42,987 --> 00:58:45,580
This is the new victim that I'm going to kill.

642
00:58:50,200 --> 00:58:52,455
Is this enough evidence?

643
00:58:59,217 --> 00:58:59,933
Look!

644
00:59:05,015 --> 00:59:07,944
Stop moving or I'll kill you live on TV!

645
00:59:10,525 --> 00:59:11,160
Look!

646
00:59:11,190 --> 00:59:12,220
(BANGKOK)

647
00:59:16,055 --> 00:59:19,273
Are you going to challenge me?
Saying that I'm not the real murderer.

648
00:59:20,010 --> 00:59:21,895
You've messed with the wrong murderer,
you stupid police!

649
00:59:23,000 --> 00:59:24,361
If you're really competent,

650
00:59:24,920 --> 00:59:26,622
come save this bitch.

651
00:59:27,560 --> 00:59:30,086
Her life depends on you guys.

652
00:59:37,610 --> 00:59:38,480
Sky!

653
00:59:42,320 --> 00:59:43,120
Shit!
